    "narrative": "The primary offensive engine for LawDog today centers on **Geraldo Perdomo** (66.51) and **Taylor Ward** (66.58), both of whom benefit from ideal matchup conditions. **Geraldo Perdomo** draws a premium matchup against M\u00e1rquez (5.64 xERA), and his promotion to the two-hole provides the optimal environment to exploit his sprint speed, which remains our highest priority category. Meanwhile, **Taylor Ward** offers the day's highest projected value; he draws a favorable park factor (+16%) and a significant platoon advantage against the lefty Boyd. While **Gavin Sheets** (62.01) is facing a tougher arm in Gallen, the 19% SP skill adjustment and his middle-of-the-order positioning make him a strong start in the current slate. \n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Dylan Beavers**, who generated a 44.00 score. Despite the benefit of the hitter-friendly park and a platoon-heavy outlook, **Dylan Beavers** was ultimately relegated to the bench due to the restrictive impact of an 8th-order placement and an opposing pitcher's high hold rate, which caps his stolen base upside\u2014our primary KPI. We are monitoring risk factors across the board, specifically noting the tough assignment for **Jung Hoo Lee** (46.14) and **Luis Arraez** (48.80) against Miles. While Miles\u2019 3.12 xERA suggests a difficult day, the wind conditions are projected to provide a marginal lift, keeping them just above our bench threshold. We continue to hold **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** on the IL, hoping for a swift return to bolster our middle-of-the-order production, while **Lawrence Butler** and **Yainer Diaz** remain on the pine as they lack starting lineup security for this afternoon\u2019s action.",
